{'question': 'A certificate chain has an untrusted root. What does the browser do?', 'choices': ['It distrusts the certificate', 'It trusts it', 'It speeds up', 'It redirects'], 'answer': 0, 'explain': 'Untrusted roots invalidate the chain.'},
{'question': 'A site serves HTTP and HTTPS with the same content. What header helps?', 'choices': ['HSTS', 'CSP', 'Cache-Control', 'ETag'], 'answer': 0, 'explain': 'HSTS forces HTTPS after the first visit.'},
{'question': 'A 401 response includes WWW-Authenticate. What does that mean?', 'choices': ['Authentication is required', 'Forbidden', 'Not found', 'Redirect'], 'answer': 0, 'explain': '401 means authentication is required.'},
{'question': "A response returns 200 but the body says 'access denied'. What is the issue?", 'choices': ['Status and body disagree; treat as a logic flaw', 'A fast page', 'A pretty page', 'A long page'], 'answer': 0, 'explain': 'Status codes and bodies should agree.'},
